From a914cf1aa3fa879b146402319054dcb3ef32dd5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:57:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: b53: rewrite the flow accelerator traps in place

b53_fa_trap_update() clears all trap rules and CFP_CTRL before it
writes the rules for the new set of ports. When a port moves to another
conduit, or the traps move to another CPU port, the ports that keep the
traps are without them until the rules are written again. The
accelerator forwards the FIN, RST and hop limit 1 frames of their flows
meanwhile, and a stats poll in that time takes their TCP and IPv6 flows
out until they are offloaded again.

Clear the rules only when the traps go off. Otherwise take the ports
that leave out of fa_trap_ports first, write the rules over the old
ones, and then set CFP_CTRL and fa_trap_ports for the new ports. Each
rule is written as a whole, so a port that keeps the traps matches every
rule at any time.

Tested on an RT-N18U: moving a port to the other conduit and back under
a UDP stream logged "flow accelerator traps to port 5" both times and no
error, and the stream went through the other conduit and back into the
accelerator as before. Throughput and the tests that take the trap
port's conduit down and up gave the same results as without this
change. With a test build, the clear took 160 us and writing the new
rules with CFP_CTRL took 196 to 268 us in twenty conduit moves (once
1 ms when the trap port's conduit came up), so before this change the
ports that keep the traps were without them for about 0.36 ms on each
move.

In a test build that stretched the window to about 4 s, TTL 1 packets
of an offloaded flow on a port that kept the traps were neither trapped
nor answered while another port moved to a new conduit. With this change
they were trapped throughout the move.

Signed-off-by: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
@@ -827,12 +827,13 @@ static void b53_fa_trap_update(struct b5
 	if (src == dev->fa_trap_ports && (!src || trap == dev->fa_trap_port))
 		return;
 
-	b53_fa_trap_clear(dev);
 	if (!src) {
+		b53_fa_trap_clear(dev);
 		dev_info(ds->dev, "flow accelerator traps off\n");
 		return;
 	}
 
+	WRITE_ONCE(dev->fa_trap_ports, dev->fa_trap_ports & src);
 	err = b53_fa_trap_set(dev, src, b53_cfp_port_bit(trap));
 	if (err) {
 		dev_err(ds->dev, "flow accelerator traps: %pe\n", ERR_PTR(err));
